 ('2702','202 0121','194','Belkin N1 Vision 4-pt Wireless Router','166.75','181.25','0.00','The N1 Vision router&#39;s easy-to-read LCD tells you everything you need to know about how your wireless network is functioning. It reports broadband speed, bandwidth usage, device usage and all connecte','2.5','y','y','','','0','36','1','The N1 Vision router&#39;s easy-to-read LCD tells you everything you need to know about how your wireless network is functioning. It reports broadband speed, bandwidth usage, device usage and all connected users. Compliant with the draft 2.0 of the forthcoming 802.11n wireless standard, it provides up to 300Mbps data transfers or an operating range up to 1,600 feet. Simple setup instructions and built-in software make it easy to get up and running. Includes CAT5 cable and AC adapter. Requires Microsoft Windows 2000/XP/Vista or Mac OS 10.4 for setup. Note: Although Belkin has designed the N1 Vision to be upgradeable to the final 802.11n specification, it may not be possible.','','belkin,802.11n,4port,4 port,4-port,wireless,router','Networking>Wireless Networking (WiFi)>Wireless Routers','P18559.jpg','P18559a.jpg','P18559a.jpg','0.00','0','0','0','0','0','0','y','n','y','n','y','y','n'),
 ('2703','202 0122','192','Netgear Rangemax Next Wireless-n USB 2.0 Adapter','89.11','96.86','0.00','NETGEAR introduces the next generation of wireless networking with the RangeMax Next products based on the proposed 802.11n amendment. While not officially ratified, the current draft permits network','0.5','y','y','','','0','242','1','NETGEAR introduces the next generation of wireless networking with the RangeMax Next products based on the proposed 802.11n amendment. While not officially ratified, the current draft permits network transmission speeds up to 300Mbps... about 6 times faster than 802.11g. This throughput allows for multiple HD video streams, video conferencing, and heavy multiplayer gaming. Draft 802.11n also increases the range of wireless network products, using multiple antennas to reach twice the distance of the previous generation. Upgrade to 802.11n with NETGEAR&#39;s RangeMax Next USB Adapter, based on the proposed draft of the new amendment. By utilizing multiple micro-antennas, it provides greater speed and range over current 802.11g. Certified to be completely compatible with existing 802.11 products, the adapter works best when used with other NETGEAR RangeMax Next products. Includes USB cable, monitor mount and software on CD-ROM. Requires Microsoft Windows XP/Vista.','','wireless,usb,wireless,rangemax,wireless-n,adapter','Networking>Wireless Networking (WiFi)>USB Wireless Adapters','P18098.jpg','P18098a.jpg','P18098a.jpg','0.00','1','0','0','0','0','0','y','n','y','n','y','y','n'),
