insert into `products` values('3695','250 0867','227','Totes Titanium Reinforced Umbrella','17.92','19.48','0.00','This stylish and lightweight umbrella uses the strength and resilience of titanium to keep you dry in the wind and rain. With its sleek two-toned handle and rubber grip finish, the umbrella opens and','1','y','y','','y','0','452','0','This stylish and lightweight umbrella uses the strength and resilience of titanium to keep you dry in the wind and rain. With its sleek two-toned handle and rubber grip finish, the umbrella opens and closes with the touch of a button. One press of the button and the canopy spreads out to its full 40 size; press button again and it collapses for quick and easy storage.','','rain,titanium,totes','Mobile Computing &amp; Travel Products>Travel Accessories','P7909.jpg','P7909a.jpg','P7909a.jpg','0.00','0','0','0','0','0','1','y','n','y','n','y','y','n'),
 ('3696','250 0966','451','12in Aluminum Frame Atomic Wall Clock','26.71','29.04','0.00','Radio-controlled (or atomic) clocks and weather stations set themselves automatically by tapping into the time signal broadcast from the cesium fountain atomic clock located in Boulder, Colorado. Ac','2.8','y','y','','y','0','218','0','Radio-controlled (or atomic) clocks and weather stations set themselves automatically by tapping into the time signal broadcast from the cesium fountain atomic clock located in Boulder, Colorado. Accurate to 1 second every 60 million years, the atomic clock signal is broadcast over North America by the National Institute of Standards and Technology. Television and radio stations, financial institutions, even NASA use this frequency for precise timekeeping! Radio-controlled clocks may have difficulty finding the NIST signal in Alaska, Hawaii, Maine and parts of Canada.','','stainless steel clock,clocks,wall clock,atomic wall clock','Office Products>Desk &amp; Wall Clocks','P11797.jpg','P11797a.jpg','P11797a.jpg','0.00','0','0','0','0','0','1','y','n','y','n','y','y','n'),
